      "id_context": "GIR-FD82-B013",
      "reported_judgment": "Actual partner participation builds a combined battle party containing shared creature identities but a separate list from the player party. Removing and boxing A shifts player members and appends the catch without updating the old combined order. Terminal item restoration visits the old combined indexes: boxed A is still reached and restored to X; live B can be emptied there and later receive Y through the shifted player index, producing the specified anomaly. Without participation the synchronized party path leaves boxed A at its current item and restores live B from the shifted old record. Registered-but-nonparticipating partner is not a counterexample. The two approved clauses in each WP20 copy correctly separate exact same-participation restoration from the capture mismatch.",
